     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d to map a multinormal distribution to normal(0,1) space</div><div>and fit with STAN.</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iris</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iris</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>E</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eigen</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%*%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> E$vectors </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%*%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">E$values</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>              </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">         </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">          </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">         </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000000e+00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.748946e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.133717e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.480081e-17</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.748946e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000000e+00</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.631728e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.908426e-15</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.133717e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.631728e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000000e+00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.630720e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.480081e-17</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.908426e-15</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.630720e-16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.000000e+00</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I generate a covariance matrix and its Eigenvalues/Eigenvectors in STAN</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quad_form_diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">L_Omega</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L_sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>coeff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eigenvectors_sym</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>eigenvals </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eigenvalues_sym</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>and then transform my Data to:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">V</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  inv_sqrt_eigenvals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  sqrt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eigenvals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  Y0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coeff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diag_matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inv_sqrt_eigenvals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>then we are able to fit Y0 to normal(0,1).</div><div><br></div><div>Since we are doing a non-linear transform, we have to adjust the jacobian:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inv_sqrt_eigenvals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Thus my question, is it the right jacobian adjustment? </div><div>The determinant of a diagonal matrix is just the product. But what about my parameter mu?</div><div><br></div><div>The inverse of <span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">coeff </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">*</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> diag_matrix</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">inv_sqrt_eigenvals</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">) is</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> diag_matrix</span><span>(1/</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">inv_sqrt_eigenvals) * transpose(coeff).</span><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></span></div><div>I&#39;m a bit confused, the manual says to take the log determinant jacobian of the <b>inverse</b> of the transform,</div><div>where STAN&#39;s warning omit the term <b>inverse.</b></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much,</div><div>Andre</div></div>"
